# UX case study demos

## Structure

- Before/after pairs in dedicated components (`*Before.jsx`, `*After.jsx`).
- Shared demo chrome wrapper for consistent framing (`CaseStudyDemoChrome`).
- Page-level narrative: eyebrow → title → subtitle → intro → interactive demo → takeaways.
- Breadcrumb back to portfolio hub on project subpages.

## Demo quality bar

- Show **realistic product UI**, not lorem-only placeholders when demonstrating a flow.
- Interactive demos should be keyboard-operable and reflect the same a11y/motion standards as production UI.
- When documenting a win, tie UI change to user outcome (fewer steps, clearer hierarchy, error recovery, etc.).

## Data density and forms

- Tables: scannable headers, sort/filter when demonstrating enterprise patterns.
- Forms: visible labels, inline validation timing, loading/submit/success/error states as part of the story.
- Empty and error states are first-class — include them in case studies when relevant.

## What to avoid in showcases

- Decorative motion with no UX purpose.
- Breaking real accessibility to make a demo look prettier.
- Scope creep into unrelated product features during a case-study fix.
